{
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "a01",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The comparison requires only distinguishing objections to an unspecified rate schedule and rate-setting date from d01’s contrast between hourly additional services and the regular retainer. The unilateral-pricing assertion need not be investigated to identify that distinction."
    },
    {
      "id": "a02",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "One look at section 1.1’s closing 'Other Tasks' language establishes the description’s cross-reference. The reviewer can then distinguish uncertainty about which tasks fall outside scope from d01’s use of the hourly-pricing limitation to construe the regular retainer."
    },
    {
      "id": "a03",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "The reviewer needs to separate the description’s notice-period payment and proration questions from d02’s stop-work route to avoiding compensation. Although both concern termination and the retainer, the description identifies its particular omissions clearly."
    },
    {
      "id": "a04",
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "score": 5,
      "estimated_minutes": 7,
      "reason": "The work is distinguishing d03’s fixed-fee-versus-draw ambiguity from d04’s contextual treatment of hours tracking, because the description expressly combines both features. The reviewer must also assess whether the final sentence about excess or unused hours changes which defect the description names."
    },
    {
      "id": "a05",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 1,
      "estimated_minutes": 1,
      "reason": "The description targets only the annual price-increase sentence and its missing procedural details. Comparing those words with the retainer-meaning and whole-contract issues in d03 and d04 is immediate."
    },
    {
      "id": "a06",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "Reading section 5.1(b) identifies the asserted monthly-versus-after-incurrence timing conflict. That complaint is readily distinguished from d05’s question whether detailed invoices imply an hourly advance retainer."
    },
    {
      "id": "a07",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 2,
      "estimated_minutes": 2,
      "reason": "The description isolates the six-percent charge’s labels and calculation base, rather than the meaning of 'Services' or the function of billable-time summaries. Its calculation assertion does not require resolution to distinguish its subject from d06 and d07."
    },
    {
      "id": "a08",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "score": 3,
      "estimated_minutes": 3,
      "reason": "The reviewer should check the two quoted timing requirements, since 'billable time' and 'full detail' also feature in the court’s retainer analysis. Once the asserted timing conflict is isolated, comparing it with d06’s compensable availability and d07’s accounting-mechanism issue is straightforward."
    },
    {
      "id": "a09",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "score": 8,
      "estimated_minutes": 18,
      "reason": "The description identifies the same stop-work and termination provisions as d08 but frames their tension as modification versus disguised termination, without identifying the advance-hourly reading or immediate cessation of compensation. The reviewer must decide whether that captures enough of the relationship the court actually construed; checking the text alone does not settle that boundary."
    }
  ]
}
